  <media:group>
   <media:title>How to Think Like Rich People (1 Hour Masterclass)</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/8WgipmPSPKk?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i1.ytimg.com/vi/8WgipmPSPKk/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>In this Kata, we discuss wealth, risk, and how rich people think about money and constraints. We talk about how money changes the way you think about time, attention, risk, and opportunity. We look at why some expenses are worth paying when they remove a major problem, and why the real question is often not “how much does this cost?” but “what does this give me back?”

We also discuss ownership, investing, and why building wealth is ultimately about separating your time and energy from the money you create. Along the way, we look at how wealthy people think about risk, where they choose to place their bets, and how they decide what is actually worth owning. 

Finally, we talk about opportunity, access, and how to think about the things that limit you. The goal is not simply to have more money, but to use it in ways that give you more time, freedom, and room to do the things that matter.

00:00 - Intro
02:39 - &quot;Blinking&quot; — teleporting into people's minds
03:48 - What rich people actually want
08:36 - Traits of every successful person
14:34 - The 4 wealth zones
15:23 - ₹1 Cr — security &amp; status
18:26 - ₹10 Cr — freedom &amp; recognition
22:57 - ₹100 Cr — influence &amp; access
30:15 - ₹1,000 Cr — legacy &amp; trust
36:56 - Free market participation
39:53 - Rich people buy freedom, not things
48:31 - How the rich take risks
54:55 - How to actually reach the rich
1:02:06 - Trust &amp; proximity to power
1:10:35 - Final summary</media:description>
